class Solution {
    public static int gcd(int a, int b) {
        if (b==0) return a;
        int rem=a%b;
        return gcd(b,rem);
    }
}


## Theory
GCD is the greatest common divisor and the optimal approach of calculating it is 
                                  
                                             
                                         GCD=GCD(b,a modulus b)
Ex:a=48 and b=18
sol)gcd=gcd(18,48%18 i.e equal to 12)
so gcd(18,12) => gcd(12,18%12 i.e equal to 6)
so gcd(12,6) =>gcd(6,12%6 i.e equal to 0) so the gcd is 6
The GCD of 48 and 18 is 6

Optimal code:

class Solution {
    public static int gcd(int a, int b) {
        while(b != 0) {
            int rem = a % b;
            a = b;
            b = rem;
        }
        return a;
    }
}

Algorithm:
1.calculate remainder
2.swap the a value with b
3.replace the b value with remainder 
4.And the gcd will be a when the remainder between a and b is 0
